# mbsync configuration — Proton Mail via Bridge → ~/.mail/proton
# Proton Bridge must be running before syncing.
# The Bridge generates a single password used for both IMAP and SMTP.
#
# Store it in Keychain once:
#   read -s -P "Bridge password: " PASS
#   security add-internet-password -s "proton-bridge" -a "neomutt" \
#     -T /usr/bin/security -w $PASS
#
# Run: mbsync -a        to sync all channels
#      mbsync proton    to sync one channel

IMAPAccount proton
Host 127.0.0.1
Port 1143
User you@proton.me
PassCmd "security find-internet-password -s 'proton-bridge' -a 'neomutt' -w 2>/dev/null | tr -d '\n'"
TLSType STARTTLS
AuthMechs LOGIN

IMAPStore proton-remote
Account proton

MaildirStore proton-local
SubFolders Verbatim
Path ~/.mail/proton/
Inbox ~/.mail/proton/INBOX

Channel proton
Far :proton-remote:
Near :proton-local:
Patterns *
Create Near
Expunge Near
SyncState *
